export const siteHtml = "<div class=\"aurora\"></div><div class=\"grain\"></div>\n<nav class=\"glass\"><div class=\"nav-in\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\"><img class=\"brandmark\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Cubbyz\"></a><div class=\"nav-links\"><a href=\"#how\">How it works</a><a href=\"#commerce\">Commerce</a><a href=\"#security\">Security</a><a href=\"#faq\">FAQ</a><a class=\"nav-cta\" href=\"#start\">Coming Soon</a></div></div></nav>\n<header class=\"hero\" id=\"top\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"tag glass\"><i></i> Trustless commerce. Secure transactions.</div>\n  <h1>Because hope is not<br><span class=\"grad\">a payment method.</span></h1>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Agree on the terms. Lock the payment. Verify the outcome. Settle by the rules.<br>\n<span style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:12px;font-size:.72em;color:var(--muted)\">Built for today's deals \u2014 and the coming world of AI agent commerce.</span></p>\n  <div class=\"hero-actions\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"#start\">Join the Cubbyz Launch</a><a class=\"btn secondary\" href=\"#demo\">See how it works</a></div>\n  <div class=\"trustbar\">\n    <div class=\"trustpill\"><b>\u2713</b> Non-custodial design</div><div class=\"trustpill\"><b>\u2713</b> USDC on Solana</div><div class=\"trustpill\"><b>\u2713</b> Blind 7-person jury</div><div class=\"trustpill\"><b>\u2713</b> Funds locked by program</div><div class=\"trustpill\"><b>\u2713</b> On-chain settlement</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"how\">\n    <div class=\"how-intro\">\n      <span class=\"how-kicker\">How a deal works</span>\n      <h2 class=\"how-title\">Transact without blind trust.</h2>\n      <p class=\"how-sub\">Whether a deal is between two people or eventually two AI agents, neither side should have to rely on blind trust. Payment is locked, the outcome is verified, and settlement follows the rules.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"howsteps\">\n      <div class=\"howstep\" data-step=\"1\">\n        <div class=\"hs-rail\"><span class=\"hs-num\">1</span><span class=\"hs-bar\"></span></div>\n        <div class=\"hs-card glass\">\n          <div class=\"hs-head\"><span class=\"hs-ic\">&#129309;</span><b>Agree</b></div>\n          <p>Buyer and seller set the terms in chat \u2014 what's delivered, and for how much.</p>\n          <span class=\"hs-tag\">takes seconds</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"howstep\" data-step=\"2\">\n        <div class=\"hs-rail\"><span class=\"hs-num\">2</span><span class=\"hs-bar\"></span></div>\n        <div class=\"hs-card glass\">\n          <div class=\"hs-head\"><span class=\"hs-ic\">&#128179;</span><b>Fund</b></div>\n          <p>Buyer funds the cubby in USDC. The payment is locked before work begins.</p>\n          <span class=\"hs-tag\">USDC on Solana</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"howstep locked-step\" data-step=\"3\">\n        <div class=\"hs-rail\"><span class=\"hs-num\">3</span><span class=\"hs-bar\"></span></div>\n        <div class=\"hs-card glass hs-locked\">\n          <div class=\"locked-visual\">\n            <div class=\"lp buyer\"><span>Buyer</span><i>can't pull it back</i></div>\n            <div class=\"lp cube\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Locked cubby\"><span class=\"lp-lock\">&#128274; LOCKED</span></div>\n            <div class=\"lp seller\"><span>Seller</span><i>can't grab it early</i></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"hs-head\"><span class=\"hs-ic\">&#128274;</span><b>Locked in the middle</b></div>\n          <p>Now it sits on-chain in a contract <strong>neither side can open alone</strong> \u2014 not the buyer, not the seller, not even Cubbyz.</p>\n          <span class=\"hs-tag green\">the trust moment</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"howstep\" data-step=\"4\">\n        <div class=\"hs-rail\"><span class=\"hs-num\">4</span><span class=\"hs-bar\"></span></div>\n        <div class=\"hs-card glass\">\n          <div class=\"hs-head\"><span class=\"hs-ic\">&#128230;</span><b>Deliver</b></div>\n          <p>Seller does the work and marks it delivered. The buyer reviews what they got.</p>\n          <span class=\"hs-tag\">buyer checks</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"howstep\" data-step=\"5\">\n        <div class=\"hs-rail\"><span class=\"hs-num\">5</span></div>\n        <div class=\"hs-card glass hs-release\">\n          <div class=\"hs-head\"><span class=\"hs-ic\">&#9989;</span><b>Released</b></div>\n          <p>Happy buyer? Funds release to the seller in seconds.</p>\n          <div class=\"branch\"><span class=\"branch-ic\">&#9878;</span><span><b>If not</b> \u2014 a blind 7-person jury settles it. 5 of 7 votes decide, executed on-chain.</span></div>\n          <span class=\"hs-tag\">~30 seconds</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"metrics\">\n  <div class=\"metrics-in\">\n    <div class=\"metric glass\"><div class=\"mnum live\">$0</div><div class=\"mlbl\">Funds lost to fraud</div><span class=\"soon\">by design</span></div>\n    <div class=\"metric glass\"><div class=\"mnum\">&lt;30s</div><div class=\"mlbl\">Typical settlement once released</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric glass\"><div class=\"mnum\">100%</div><div class=\"mlbl\">Of locked funds held on-chain</div></div>\n    <div class=\"metric glass\"><div class=\"mnum\">5 / 7</div><div class=\"mlbl\">Blind juror votes to settle a dispute</div></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</header>\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"demo\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"kicker\">Interactive demo</div><h2>Watch a Cubby close.</h2><p>A single deal moves from agreement, to locked funds, to delivery, to release or jury settlement.</p></div>\n<div class=\"app glass\"><div class=\"app-top\"><span class=\"dot\"></span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span class=\"app-title mono\">cubbyz://deal/CBZ-00120</span><span class=\"net mono\">SOLANA DEVNET</span></div><div class=\"stage\"><div class=\"steps\">\n<button class=\"step active\" data-i=\"0\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span><span class=\"t\">Create cubby</span><span class=\"s\">terms + amount</span></span></button>\n<button class=\"step\" data-i=\"1\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span><span class=\"t\">Lock payment</span><span class=\"s\">buyer funds vault</span></span></button>\n<button class=\"step\" data-i=\"2\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span><span class=\"t\">Deliver work</span><span class=\"s\">seller completes</span></span></button>\n<button class=\"step\" data-i=\"3\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span><span class=\"t\">Release or dispute</span><span class=\"s\">buyer decision</span></span></button>\n<button class=\"step\" data-i=\"4\"><span class=\"num\">5</span><span><span class=\"t\">Settle</span><span class=\"s\">on-chain result</span></span></button>\n</div><div class=\"screen\">\n<div class=\"scr on\" data-s=\"0\"><h3>Set the terms.</h3><p class=\"desc\">The buyer and seller agree on scope, amount, deadline, and release conditions before payment is locked.</p><div class=\"field\"><label>Deal</label><div class=\"inp\"><span>Logo package</span><span class=\"cur\">CBZ-00120</span></div></div><div class=\"field\"><label>Amount</label><div class=\"inp\"><span>$120.00</span><span class=\"cur\">USDC</span></div></div><button class=\"btn\" data-act=\"create\">Create cubby</button><div class=\"statusbar mono\" id=\"st0\"></div></div>\n<div class=\"scr\" data-s=\"1\"><h3>Payment locks instantly.</h3><p class=\"desc\">The buyer pays in. Money leaves their balance, but the seller cannot touch it until release or verdict.</p><div class=\"bigamt\"><span class=\"grad\">$120.00</span></div><button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"fund()\">Lock USDC</button><div class=\"statusbar mono\" id=\"st1\"></div></div>\n<div class=\"scr\" data-s=\"2\"><h3>Both sides can see the vault.</h3><p class=\"desc\">The seller starts work because the money is already present. The buyer stays protected because it remains locked.</p><div class=\"vault-vis\"><div class=\"vparty\"><div class=\"av\">\ud83d\udc64</div><div class=\"nm\">Buyer</div></div><div class=\"flowline\"></div><div class=\"vcore\" id=\"vcore\"><div class=\"lock-ic\">\ud83d\udd12</div><div class=\"vlabel mono\">LOCKED</div></div><div class=\"flowline\"></div><div class=\"vparty\"><div class=\"av\">\ud83c\udfa8</div><div class=\"nm\">Seller</div></div></div><button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"go(3)\">Work delivered</button></div>\n<div class=\"scr\" data-s=\"3\"><h3>Release or escalate.</h3><p class=\"desc\">If the work is accepted, funds release to the seller. If not, the dispute is routed to a blind 7-person jury.</p><div class=\"btn-row\"><button class=\"btn\" onclick=\"release()\">Release funds</button><button class=\"btn secondary\" onclick=\"dispute()\">Open dispute</button></div><div class=\"statusbar mono\" id=\"st3\"></div></div>\n<div class=\"scr\" data-s=\"4\"><div id=\"settleBox\" style=\"text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:46px;margin-bottom:8px\">\ud83c\udf89</div><h3>Deal settled.</h3><p class=\"desc\" style=\"margin:8px auto 16px\">The final action executes on-chain and closes the cubby.</p><button class=\"replay mono\" onclick=\"reset()\">\u21bb run it again</button></div></div>\n</div></div></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"how\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"kicker\">Why it works</div><h2>Simple enough for normal users. Strong enough for crypto deals.</h2></div><div class=\"grid3\"><div class=\"card glass\"><div class=\"ic\">\ud83d\udcb3</div><h3>USDC on Solana</h3><p>Fund a cubby with USDC on Solana, with fast confirmation and low transaction costs.</p></div><div class=\"card glass\"><div class=\"ic\">\ud83d\udd10</div><h3>Payment locked before work</h3><p>The seller sees that payment is locked before delivering. Release follows the agreed transaction rules.</p></div><div class=\"card glass\"><div class=\"ic\">\u2696\ufe0f</div><h3>Disputes have a path</h3><p>A blind jury mechanism gives users a fallback when the buyer and seller cannot agree.</p></div></div></div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"settlement\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">Settlement primitive</div>\n    <h2>Agree. Fund. Verify. Settle.</h2>\n    <p style=\"color:var(--muted);max-width:720px;margin-top:12px\">\n      Cubbyz turns a deal into explicit rules so payment does not depend on one side simply trusting the other.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"flowline\">\n    <div class=\"flowbox\"><b>1 \u00b7 Agree</b><span>Define the amount, deliverable, deadline, and settlement rules.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"flowbox\"><b>2 \u00b7 Fund</b><span>Lock payment before the seller or service provider performs the work.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"flowbox\"><b>3 \u00b7 Verify</b><span>Confirm completion through mutual approval, evidence, or future machine-verifiable checks.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"flowbox\"><b>4 \u00b7 Settle</b><span>Release, refund, split, expire, or route the transaction into dispute resolution.</span></div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"commerce\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">AI agent commerce</div>\n    <h2>Commerce does not stop with humans.</h2>\n    <p style=\"color:var(--muted);max-width:760px;margin-top:12px\">\n      Cubbyz is designed around a simple settlement primitive that works whether the counterparties are people, AI agents, or both.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"vision-grid\">\n    <div class=\"vision-card glass\">\n      <div class=\"pair\">Human \u2194 Human</div>\n      <h3>Deals without blind trust.</h3>\n      <p>Lock payment before work begins, verify the result, then release or dispute according to the agreed rules.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"vision-card glass\">\n      <div class=\"pair\">Human \u2194 Agent</div>\n      <h3>Delegate with payment protection.</h3>\n      <p>People can authorize AI agents to perform work while payment remains tied to explicit outcomes instead of promises.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"vision-card glass\">\n      <div class=\"pair\">Agent \u2194 Agent</div>\n      <h3>Autonomous commerce with guardrails.</h3>\n      <p>AI agents can hire, pay, verify, and settle with other AI agents using programmable payment controls and machine-readable transaction rules.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"vision-note glass\">The counterparty does not have to be human. <span class=\"grad\">The rules stay the same.</span></div>\n</div>\n\n\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"disputes\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">When both sides disagree</div>\n    <h2>Disputes need a process, not a shouting match.</h2>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"dispute-grid\">\n    <div class=\"dispute-card glass\">\n      <h3>Escalation is part of the protocol.</h3>\n      <p>If the parties cannot settle directly, the cubby can move into a dispute state instead of leaving payment trapped in an informal argument.</p>\n      <div class=\"dispute-steps\">\n        <div class=\"dispute-step\"><i>01</i><div><b>Freeze settlement</b><br><span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">Funds stay locked while the dispute is reviewed.</span></div></div>\n        <div class=\"dispute-step\"><i>02</i><div><b>Submit evidence</b><br><span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">Each side provides the relevant transaction context and proof.</span></div></div>\n        <div class=\"dispute-step\"><i>03</i><div><b>Blind jury review</b><br><span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">Seven independent jurors evaluate the dispute without public pressure.</span></div></div>\n        <div class=\"dispute-step\"><i>04</i><div><b>Settle by verdict</b><br><span style=\"color:var(--muted)\">The outcome follows the defined settlement rules.</span></div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"dispute-card glass\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">Why this matters</div>\n      <h3>A fallback changes the deal before anything goes wrong.</h3>\n      <p>When both parties know there is a defined path for disagreement, neither side has to rely on threats, reputation alone, or off-platform promises.</p>\n      <p style=\"margin-top:14px\">For agent commerce, the same principle applies: AI agents need deterministic escalation and settlement behavior when verification is ambiguous or contested.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"security\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"security\"><div class=\"panel glass\"><div class=\"kicker\">Trust model</div><h2>Trust the rules, not the stranger.</h2><p>Cubbyz makes the security model visible before anyone funds a deal. The product is built around program-controlled payments, clear release rules, and a transparent dispute path.</p></div><div class=\"panel glass\"><div class=\"security-list\"><div class=\"security-item\"><b>Non-custodial transactions</b><span>Funds are locked by the transaction program rather than held in a Cubbyz-operated wallet.</span></div><div class=\"security-item\"><b>Program-enforced release</b><span>Funds only move after release, expiry logic, or a dispute verdict.</span></div><div class=\"security-item\"><b>Blind 7-person jury</b><span>Jurors are randomly selected and review disputes without public pressure; a majority verdict determines settlement.</span></div><div class=\"security-item\"><b>Transparent by design</b><span>Program addresses, transaction activity, and transaction settlement can be independently verified on-chain.</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>\n\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"boundaries\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">What Cubbyz is building</div>\n    <h2>A settlement layer, not another middleman.</h2>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"boundary-grid\">\n    <div class=\"boundary-card glass\">\n      <h3>What Cubbyz does</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Locks payment under explicit transaction rules</li>\n        <li>Creates a verifiable settlement path</li>\n        <li>Supports mutual release and dispute escalation</li>\n        <li>Provides primitives that can be used by people or AI agents</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"boundary-card glass\">\n      <h3>What Cubbyz does not ask you to do</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Send money first and hope the other side performs</li>\n        <li>Trust Cubbyz employees to manually hold your funds</li>\n        <li>Depend only on screenshots, reputation, or chat promises</li>\n        <li>Use a human counterparty for every transaction</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"faq\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"kicker\">FAQ</div><h2>Questions before using a cubby.</h2></div>\n  <div class=\"faq\">\n    <details><summary>What is Cubbyz?</summary><p>Cubbyz is a trustless commerce and settlement platform. It lets counterparties agree on terms, lock payment, verify the outcome, and settle according to explicit rules.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>Does Cubbyz hold user funds?</summary><p>Cubbyz is designed so locked funds are controlled by program rules rather than a manual Cubbyz withdrawal process.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>What happens if both sides agree?</summary><p>The transaction follows the agreed release path and settles without a dispute.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>What happens if there is a dispute?</summary><p>The transaction can be frozen and routed into Cubbyz's dispute process, where evidence is reviewed and the outcome follows the defined settlement rules.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>Is Cubbyz only for Telegram deals?</summary><p>No. Telegram is an initial user experience, not the boundary of the platform. The underlying commerce and settlement model is intended to support additional interfaces and integrations.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>Is Cubbyz only for people?</summary><p>No. The same transaction model can support human-to-human, human-to-agent, and agent-to-agent commerce.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>What currency will Cubbyz use?</summary><p>The initial implementation uses USDC for settlement. Additional payment and integration options can be added as the platform expands.</p></details>\n    <details><summary>Is Cubbyz live?</summary><p>Cubbyz is currently preparing for launch. Public access, program addresses, production documentation, and final risk disclosures will be published before users are asked to fund live transactions.</p></details>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n\n\n<section class=\"final\" id=\"start\"><div class=\"wrap\">\n  <div class=\"launch-card glass\">\n    <div class=\"eyebrow\">Coming soon</div>\n    <h2>Commerce without blind trust.</h2>\n    <p>Cubbyz is building a transaction layer for deals that need more than a promise \u2014 from people doing business with strangers to autonomous agents transacting with each other.</p>\n    <div class=\"launch-pills\">\n      <span class=\"launch-pill\">Human \u2194 Human</span>\n      <span class=\"launch-pill\">Human \u2194 Agent</span>\n      <span class=\"launch-pill\">Agent \u2194 Agent</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></section>\n\n\n<footer>\n  <div class=\"mono\">Cubbyz \u00b7 trustless commerce \u00b7 coming soon</div>\n  <div class=\"footer-links\">\n    <span>Terms at launch</span>\n    <span>Privacy at launch</span>\n    <span>Risk disclosures at launch</span>\n    <span>Developer docs at launch</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:12px;opacity:.55\">\u00a9 2026 Cubbyz. All rights reserved.</div>\n</footer>";
